From peter.jeremy at alcatel.com.au  Wed Apr  2 16:17:59 2003
From: peter.jeremy at alcatel.com.au (Peter Jeremy)
Date: Wed Apr  2 16:18:00 2003
Subject: mylex dac960pu on alpha
In-Reply-To: <200304021208.h32C8D0j020495@satanii.enemy.org>
References: <200304021208.h32C8D0j020495@satanii.enemy.org>
Message-ID: <20030403001750.GW310@gsmx07.alcatel.com.au>

On 2003-Apr-02 14:08:13 +0200, "Chris J. Mutter" <cjm@s2.enemy.org> wrote:
>i have a question to the dac960pu: can this controller under firmware
>2.x work with LVD drives bigger than 9gig? i would like to know this
>before i order drives. 

If this is a KZPAC-AA or KZPAC-CA then you can use drives >9GB but I
don't think it supports LVD.  We have tried both 18GB and 36GB drives
and both work as JBOD drives - but the 36GB drive is limited to 32GB
(the block addresses wrap at 26 bits).  I haven't tried mirroring
(though I'd expect that to work) or creating multiple logical drives
on a single physical drive.

Peter
